    "question": {
      ":question/id": "bfc68284-d14f-54a1-bea9-e889225a72b2",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x + 2 y &=1 \\\\ - 3 x - y + 5 z &=17 \\\\ - 2 x - 4 y + z &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -1 & 5 & 17 \\\\ -2 & -4 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -1 & 5 & 17 \\\\ -2 & -4 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 5 & 20 \\\\ -2 & -4 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 5 & 20 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{3} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-3 \\\\ y &=2 \\\\ z &=2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSo, we have the solution $x=-3$, $y=2$, and $z=2.$ Or, in vector form, $\\langle -3,2,2\\rangle$.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
