    "question": {
      ":question/id": "767fb150-b6b1-5850-bf17-1dc0a5e83e88",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x - y + 2 z &=9 \\\\ 3 x - 2 y + 6 z &=29 \\\\ - 2 x + 2 y - z &=-6\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 2 & 9 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 6 & 29 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -1 & -6\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 2 & 9 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 6 & 29 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -1 & -6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 2 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -1 & -6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 2 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 12\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{3} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 2 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{3} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
