    "question": {
      ":question/id": "ef3f1230-602d-544c-8647-4e0cfff8097c",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x - 3 y &=-8 \\\\ y + 2 z &=9 \\\\ 5 x - 7 y + 17 z &=29\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 9 \\\\ 5 & -7 & 17 & 29\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 9 \\\\ 5 & -7 & 17 & 29\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 17 & 69\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-8){R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{3} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 15 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+3{R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 0 & 37 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 15 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -3\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
